WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:02.350
Thank you.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:04.580
Yes.

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:05.990
is Beverly Hill.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.260
Here dwelled the rich.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:09.500
The famous.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.020
The Glamouries.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.580
Movie stars.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.560
Royalty and exile.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.600
Retired Millionaire.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.160
Sportsman.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.360
Playboys.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:20.940
Hillbillies?

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.500
Hillbillies?

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.340
Who are these people?

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.190
Where are they from?

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.680
And why did they come to Beverly Hills?

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.720
We'll discover the answers in a moment as we bring you The Hillbilly.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.660
Come on, let's find that house we bought.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.230
House they bought?

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.560
In Beverly Hills?

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.510
Whoa, wait a minute, hold it!

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.460
Enough with a bunch of hillbillies,

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.540
possibly by a mansion like this.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.930
Let's take them back to their home in the Ozarks

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.810
and see how this whole thing started.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:49.310
Not that youngin' he yearn.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:52.910
fighting with a bobcat.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:53.850
It hurt?

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.180
I reckon so.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.520
It went limp and off on three legs.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.440
I don't know what to do about that girl.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.400
Well, the first thing to do is to get her into a dress.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.330
She's getting too big to be wearing man's duds.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.460
Looky here.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.180
She's done popped the buttons off of her shirt again.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.280
Well, everybody carries herself proud,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.170
with her shoulders thrown back.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.340
It ain't her shoulders that's popping these buttons.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.720
Some boy will come along and start courting the urn.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.770
They came courting when she was 12.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.140
What did she do?

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.650
She whooped the tar on him.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.370
A girl running around as wild as a cougar.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.000
Wrestling, fighting, and hunting.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:49.510
She ought to be doing woman's work.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.540
Happened me with the steel.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:55.580
I speak to her.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:56.840
Oh

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.880
That reminds me.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:04.590
Better go down and stomp out the fire under that mesh.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.760
You ain't gonna stomp out no fire like that, are you?

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:11.300
Huh?

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:13.460
Oh!

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.580
Of course not, don't want to burn the shoes.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:29.520
What you got there?

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:32.110
Stranger.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:34.410
Where'd you get him?

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.680
Get him with a rock.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.530
He was skooking around down by the slough.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.240
Figured he might be a revenuer.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:43.310
He ain't no revenuer.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.670
Then can I keep him?

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.670
Of course not. Well, I called him.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.270
That don't matter. Well, he won't be no trouble.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.090
I could keep him out in the smokehouse.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.610
Ellie Mae, you can't keep people

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.290
like they were dogs and cats.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.570
Fella Ellie found nosin' around.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.780
Bein' it worth a rock, so it'd be easier to tote.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.060
There are fellas from the Petroleum Company.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.490
What's a Petroleum?

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:23.650
I don't know.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.980
He asked me if he could do some wildcatting down by the slough.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.500
I said, help yourself.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.980
We're glad to get rid of the crib.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.380
The last on him, there ain't no wildcats down there at that slough.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:38.820
Heck no. It's too full of oil.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.760
Oh, what happened?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:51.310
This here is the Clampett place. I'm Jed Clampett, my youngin' Ellie Mae and Granny.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.330
Granny says you've been doin' some wildcatin'.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.980
There's no need to. Mr. Clampett, that swamp of yours is full of oil.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:04:59.960
I could've told you.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.200
that well my company would like to pump it out yeah i'd like that too but i just can't afford to

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:13.140
have it done you don't understand you see you wouldn't have to pay for it oh i don't take favors

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:22.640
from strangers no no no mr clampett you see uh you're a very rich man how big a rock did you be

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:29.980
listen i've got to call my office in tulsa have you got to tell

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.310
A what?

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:32.950
A telephone.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.930
Well, maybe one of your neighbors has one.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:36.610
It's a...

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.390
Well, down in this country, it's probably a box attached to the wall.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.520
And you talk into it, and they can hear you in Tulsa.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.310
Sit down for a spell.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.340
No, I haven't time.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.040
Listen, where's the nearest airfield?

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.180
Airfield?

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.900
You know, Granny, that's one of them airfields sets up in the air.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.380
Listen, now don't you sell that swamp till you hear from me.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.250
I'm flying to Tulsa.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:13.960
Now he thinks he's got wings.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.260
Watch them buttons, John.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:39.830
Sears got into the corn.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:43.360
Did they drink much?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.510
I reckon they did. This here little fella

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.270
was kicking blue blazes out of the mule.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.390
Trouble with razorbacks?

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.490
They such a mean drunk.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:19.700
I'd say that's gonna be one of the richest pools since East Texas.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.620
News like this is bound to get out.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.840
Let's go down and get Pappin's name on a deal.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.450
You want to see what just flew over Blueberry Rich?

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:34.790
What?

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:38.010
The dad blamed this biggest bird you ever laid eyes on him.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.770
Well, he's just an overrode chicken hawk.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:40.790
Chicken hawk? Nothing?

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:42.470
That thing could make off of the hog.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:43.850
Hurry up, put that gun together.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.600
Land near the cabin, Mr. Brewster.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.500
It's too rocky and hilly.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.680
Then let's get the sling ready to be lowered.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.880
Well, Mr. Brewster, that might be dangerous.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:56.880
Hang the danger.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.660
We're going to be the first oil company down there if it kills you.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:04.160
Me? Don't worry. If it's safe, I'll follow you.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:07.750
Penny, I...

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:08.360
Yes!

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:10.980
See, look at that.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:13.990
Whatcha doin', Granny?

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.810
That thing's only got one claw,

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:17.490
but dang it if it ain't grabbed up a man.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.050
Thank you.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:21.770
Thank you.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:24.170
Thank you.

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:25.660
Origins.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.850
Just roll in the house. I'll give it on to the side.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:42.170
No, but I'm a stranger.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:10.880
something and hang on cousin pearl and that overgrown son of hers is headed right for the

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.520
cabin in that old truck him and protect us

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.780
I think they sure want the chicken house.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:35.530
I'm sure it's all about the chicken house, but nobody got hurt.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:37.670
You

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:41.930
Jethro, I told you to get rid of them worn-out brakes.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.970
I did, Ma. That's how come we ain't got to it.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:47.700
Get out!

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.110
He left the chicken mouth back on his foundation.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:57.380
Chad, Ellie May came running over to my place and she said you sold the swamp to some art company.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:09:59.720
Yeah.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.930
Yeah, I guess I did.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:05.070
What did they pay you for?

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:08.060
They ain't paid me nothing yet.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.520
The rooster fella said he'd bring the money later.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:11.980
How much they gonna pay you?

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:14.780
Well, he said I'd...

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.110
Depends on how much oil they could pump out.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:19.900
He must have mentioned some figure. What was it?

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.020
Now, Pearl, you know that old swamp one.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:27.670
You got slick and you're ashamed to admit it.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.340
That's just what I told you.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.000
How much they gonna pay him?

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:32.260
All right, I'll tell you.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.400
He said it runs somewhere between $25 and $100.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:35.580
$25 and $100?

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:42.390
I know it don't sound like much, but Mr. Brewster seems to set great store by the fact he's going to pay me in some new kind of dollar.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.640
There ain't no new kind of dollar.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:50.470
Well, it's new to me. I've heard of gold dollars, silver dollars, paper dollars.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:53.430
But he says he's going to pay me in, uh, what do you call them, Granny?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:55.730
Million dollars

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:07.760
Here you can sit for yourself. I don't care about that.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:09.520
Sit here.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.260
Thanks in heaven.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:16.290
Granny, give me the jug.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.770
It's empty, but I'll fetch some.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:19.590
There you go, Granny.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:28.010
Hey, check it. You're a millionaire.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:29.850
A millionaire.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.530
That's what that Brewster fella kept calling me.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.050
I didn't know just how to take it.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.430
He meant you're rich.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:38.640
Me?

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:41.130
The richest man in these hills.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:42.760
Maybe in the whole state.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:46.860
Oh, Jed, you can have anything you want.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.680
Do anything you want.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:50.560
Go any place you want.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.930
Yeah, that's another thing he kept saying.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:55.660
He said he reckoned I'd be moving away from here soon.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.020
What do you think, Pearl? You think I ought to move?

00:11:59.500 --> 00:11:59.880
Jed.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.740
How can you even ask?

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:03.340
Look around you.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.190
You're eight miles from your nearest neighbor.

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:10.910
You're overrun with skunks, possums, coyotes, bald cats.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.640
You use kerosene lamps for light.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.860
You cook on a wood stove summer and winter.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.310
You're drinking homemade moonshine,

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.390
washing with homemade lye soap.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.830
And your bathroom is 50 feet from the house

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.050
and you ask, should you move?

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:33.970
You'd be a dang fool to leave all this.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.570
Dad, you misunderstood me.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.390
I meant you should move away.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:54.960
And you know where I'd go if I was you?

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:55.380
Where?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:57.440
California.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:12:59.190
California?

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.520
Yes, sir. Beverly Hills, California.

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:09.720
Jed, remember the time that your pa took us to Eureka Springs to see the movie picture?

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:11.930
Yeah.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:17.700
Well, the actors that make their movie pictures live in Beverly Hills.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:20.440
Yes, sir.

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:23.450
Well, doggies.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.920
Living in the same neck of the woods with old-town me.

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:44.850
And we could come visit you. You know what else they say about California? What? You don't get cold out there. What don't get cold out there?

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:49.190
Nothing don't get cold out there. They don't have no snow or no water.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:50.700
Didn't he bring some in?

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:53.430
They don't want it.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:59.840
Remember last winter when she slipped on the ice and broke her hip?

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.940
Yeah, poor old woman. She was limping for two days.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:11.200
That couldn't happen in California because they don't have no eyes.

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:12.230
How come?

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:18.360
I don't know how come, but Grinny sure like it, and we could visit you.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.130
You know what they say about California?

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:29.410
Maybe Jethro know how come there's no eyes. He's going to school.

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:31.300
We could ask you.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:33.730
Yes, sir?

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:35.150
Yeah, Ma?

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.230
Come on over here.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:43.120
Speaking of school, Ellie Mae could get herself a fine education out there in Beverly Hill.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:43.780
Yeah, Ma?

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:48.280
Your rich uncle's got a question he'd like to ask you.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.130
What rich uncle, Ma?

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.540
Rich Uncle Jay.

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:57.000
Jethro, how come there's no ice in California?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:01.740
Don't look at me. I didn't take it.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:16.010
Say, Jeth, folks claim California's got it all beat.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:19.050
Why, things grow twice as big out there.

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.780
Jethro would be a whopper, wouldn't he?

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:26.450
He could help you move.

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.970
He's awful handy at lifting and toting, and he could drive...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:38.440
out in my truck now I couldn't let you do that yeah we're kinfolk what's mine is

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:45.300
yours and then I could come out later and and ride back with him and and bring

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:57.380
his unmarried sister along we could visit for a while yeah tell you about them

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.840
oranges they grow up

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:04.000
I'm going to have to study on this.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.860
When that Brewster fella comes back, I'll ask him what he thinks.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:12.140
Well, your cousin is right about that, Mr. Plampett.

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.490
Beverly Hills is a choice residential area,

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.000
and lots of millionaires do settle there.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:18.380
Folks like me, huh?

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.900
Well, uh, millionaires.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:23.400
And movie stars, too.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:24.180
Oh, yes, yes.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.420
Is Tom Mix there?

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:28.940
No, I'm afraid Mr. Mix is dead.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.480
Oh, yeah. What's the matter with me?

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.160
Remember, Pearl? He got shot at the end of that picture.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:46.260
And that's where Jed wants to live. Ain't it, Jed?

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:50.840
I do like the notion of living in the hills.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:53.340
Never could stand flat country.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:56.090
Mr. Clampett, I think it only fair.

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:59.970
That is, well, I think you may have a wrong...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.360
idea about Beverly Hill. Is that where you live? No, my home is in Tulsa. Oh, say, maybe you could

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:13.210
get us a place there in your neighborhood. Mr. Clampett, let's not beat around the bush. You

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:21.160
will love Beverly Hill. The magic. Can you steer Jade onto a good place? No, I can get the bank out

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:27.990
there to handle it for him. He'd like a nice big place with plenty of room for his kinfolk to visit him.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.140
I would like a nice roomy place if I could afford it.

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:40.360
Oh, Mr. Clampett, with your money, you can afford the Taj Mahal.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.600
Okay, I'll take it.

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:45.730
Well, no, you see, I was just making a little joke.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:48.430
Oh, well, go right ahead.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:53.810
Well, you see, the Taj Mahal is in India.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:04.880
Mr. Brewster, you're a nice fellow, but I heard better jokes.

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:10.510
Is the foreigner staying to supper?

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:13.420
I'm ashamed to say I ain't asked him. How about it?

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.140
Oh, I don't think so.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:16.420
Oh, no trouble.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:17.600
What you cooking tonight, Granny?

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.760
Mustard greens and possum innards.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.460
You hear that, Mr. Brewster?

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:25.960
Very clever.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:29.860
Uh, not.

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:34.430
If you could happen to come back tomorrow, we'll be having leftovers.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:38.230
